<rdf:Description rdf:about="Definition-64538">
<zthes:label>Mars orbiter mission designed to make global observations of Mars to improve our understanding of the Martian climate and geologic history, including the search for liquid water and evidence of past life. The three primary instruments carried onboard are THEMIS (Thermal Emission Imaging System), GRS (Gamma Ray Spectrometer), and MARIE (Mars Radiation Environment Experiment). Launched April 2001.</zthes:label>
</rdf:Description>
